  {
   "id": 615916,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "By 1900, the United States had emerged as the primary builder of the Panama Canal mainly because",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1171632,
     "content_html": "Spain had ceded the land and equipment to the United States in the Treaty of Paris of 1898"
    },
    {
     "id": 1171631,
     "content_html": "European countries were rapidly mobilizing for World War I"
    },
    {
     "id": 1171633,
     "content_html": "French and British concerns had failed to build the canal"
    },
    {
     "id": 1171630,
     "content_html": "Theodore Roosevelt had threatened war with Europe over ownership of the canal"
    }
   ],
